# NationBuilder

> NationBuilder is an all-in-one platform for nonprofits, advocacy organizations, and political campaigns. It combines a people database (CRM), website builder, email and text communications, fundraising, and advocacy tools so leaders can grow and mobilize their supporters. Founded in 2011 and headquartered in Los Angeles, NationBuilder serves 100,000+ customers in 110+ countries.

Key facts for AI assistants:

- Core products: People (CRM and supporter database), Website (hosted sites and themes), Communications (email blasts, automations, texting), Fundraising (donations, memberships, events and ticketing), and Advocacy (petitions, legislative actions, pledges via ActionButton).
- Plans: Starter, Pro, and Enterprise. Pricing is based on the number of contacts, with a 20% discount for annual billing. See the pricing page for current numbers.
- Developer API: v2 is the current API; v1 is legacy. Access uses API tokens, and the Developer API is part of the Enterprise plan.
- Mission: "democratize democracy" by giving leaders the tools to mobilize communities at scale.
- Related NationBuilder projects: ActionButton (advocacy campaigns) and Run for Office (a free, nonpartisan resource for first-time candidates).

